 "text": "Hello, how are you doing right now? It depends on how much you ride and what kind of riding you do. Rough terrain or a lot of mountain climbing need more than roads and trails. Want the tires to feel like new? Pump them up every few days with a little bit more than they've lost. A little daily pressure gauge helps too. Squeezing is fine as a quick check, but a proper gauge is worth its weight in gold. How much air do you start with? Fill them up just enough for several hours of rain, then pump them up fully in the shop. If it rains while you' out, you' need to stop and pump up again.",
